// Part of the specification: components, relationships.
{
  "components": [
    {
      "id": "tooling",
      "name": "Tooling",
      "kind": "subsystem",
      "category": "infrastructure",
      "purpose": "Build and development system, verification pipeline, artifact generators, tests and development utilities.",
      "implementation": {
        "status": "manual",
        "modules": [],
        "notes": "Grouping only; the code lives in the child components.",
        "language": "js"
      },
      "parent": "exegra",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Build and serve the application and its engines (build system, Rust oracle build).",
        "Execute the evidence the claims name and record the outcomes with the stamp of the tree they ran on, and compare declared modules with the files on disk (verification pipeline).",
        "Generate the derived artifacts of a project deterministically from its model (generators).",
        "Test the semantic core, the command line and the running application, and capture screenshots of it (test suites, screenshot tool).",
        "Import specifications kept as Markdown, generate synthetic benchmarks, and realise projects whose code lives in other repositories."
      ]
    },
    // ======== Tooling ========================================================================
    {
      "id": "build-system",
      "name": "Build and development system",
      "parent": "tooling",
      "category": "infrastructure",
      "runsIn": "node",
      "purpose": "Vite configuration: serves the application on 127.0.0.1 with the development-server plugin, builds a static bundle with relative asset URLs, and keeps saved specifications from triggering page reloads. The Pages workflow, triggered by a push to main, publishes that bundle, which opens Exegra's own specification first, to the repository's GitHub Pages site.",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Build a static bundle whose asset URLs are relative, so it loads at a domain root or under the repository's GitHub Pages sub-path",
        "Declare the Pages workflow (.github/workflows/pages.yml): triggered by a push to main, it builds the Lean core to WebAssembly, validates Exegra's own specification, builds and uploads the bundle and deploys it to GitHub Pages; in a run whose specification does not validate nothing is published"
      ],
      "unknowns": [
        "Only the workflow file is checked (tests/core/pages-site.test.js): that GitHub runs it, and that every push to main is published, are not. Under the workflow's concurrency group a queued run is replaced when a newer push arrives, so an intermediate push may never be deployed; a disabled workflow, Pages not set to GitHub Actions or a push marked to skip CI publish nothing.",
        "The GitHub Pages site is the production build: read-only, it shows the specifications as of the last push to main with the evidence results recorded in specs/exegra/evidence/results.json, and, the Lean core being wasm64, it does not run in stable Safari.",
        "The production build contains no persistence service: it bundles the shipped specs and is read-only.",
        "dist/ embeds as text the specification, layout and recorded results of every shipped project and the specification of every linked project whose specification lives outside specs/ (copy shipped-specifications); a linked project's specification, which is not in this repository, therefore ends up in the build output (WG-4775, finding F11)."
      ],
      "implementation": {
        "status": "manual",
        "modules": [
          "vite.config.js",
          ".github/workflows/pages.yml",
          ".github/workflows/check.yml"
        ],
        "notes": "package.json scripts (dev, build, test, test:browser, typecheck, exegra, generate, verify) are not a scanned source file.",
        "language": "js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "generators",
      "name": "Artifact generators",
      "parent": "tooling",
      "category": "logical",
      "runsIn": "both",
      "purpose": "Deterministic pure functions from the model, claim results and diagnostics to five artifacts: manifest.json, ARCHITECTURE.md, claims-report.md, claims-report.json and tasks.json.",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Derive each artifact byte-identically from the same inputs, without reading the file system, the clock or the environment",
        "Report a claim without a result as not evaluated, never as verified",
        "Derive a task list from violated and unevaluated claims, validation errors, not-implemented components, traceability findings, unknowns and gaps",
        "Generate the capability matrix (capabilities.md): per guarantee class the claims Lean shows established (proved, fresh, no open assumption) and the others with their status, and the counts of the specification"
      ],
      "unknowns": ["No generator emits code or any part of Exegra's own runtime; Exegra generates reports about the model, not the software it describes."],
      "implementation": {
        "status": "manual",
        "modules": [
          "src/core/generate/architecture-doc.js",
          "src/core/generate/capabilities.js",
          "src/core/generate/claims-report.js",
          "src/core/generate/index.js",
          "src/core/generate/manifest.js",
          "src/core/generate/task-manifest.js"
        ],
        "language": "js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verification-pipeline",
      "name": "Verification pipeline",
      "parent": "tooling",
      "category": "logical",
      "runsIn": "node",
      "purpose": "Compares the implementation modules that components declare with the files on disk and, driven by `exegra verify`, executes test evidence and records the results.",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Report declared modules missing on disk and files under src, cli and tools (.js, .json, .css, .html) plus index.html and vite.config.js that no component claims, leaving out generated build output (src/engine/pkg/) and files whose name starts with local- (local data, ignored by git)",
        "Through `verify`: validate, check traceability, execute each evidence of kind test with node --test or Playwright and record outcomes and the traceability result in results.json, then re-evaluate claims with them",
        "Refuse an evidence reference with characters outside letters, digits, underscore, dot, slash, hyphen, space, hash and colon, and time a test run out after ten minutes",
        "Reuse the outcomes that `npm test` and `npm run test:browser` already recorded (reporters in tools/ writing .outcomes/, each stamped with a hash over the tracked files, the untracked files git does not ignore and the generated engine builds) instead of running the same test again: an evidence reference is answered from the recorded run only when the run was complete, the tree did not change during it and its stamp equals the stamp of the tree verify runs on; a reference that matches no recorded test, a failure, or a skipped browser test is run as before, and a unit test that skipped itself is recorded as skipped. results.json says for each outcome whether it was run or reused; `verify --fresh` reuses nothing",
        "Decide what a reference's matched tests establish with one function on the fresh path (node's TAP output, Playwright's summary) and the reuse path (the recorded outcomes) alike: only leaf tests count, a describe block is not a test, todo tests are recorded as todo, and a reference passes only when at least one matched test executed and passed and none failed, skipped or is a todo",
        "Stamp what it records: the records stamp (the tree stamp without specs/<project>/evidence/results.json and specs/<project>/generated/) on every evidence result, and on every Lean theorem check the hash of the formal/ sources checked, the records stamp and the sha256 of the theorem statement as Lean printed it",
        "Scan the imports of every module a component claims (tools/import-scan.js) and record the outcome for the assumption relationships-match-imports: refuted when an import between components, or a module reaching the file system, has no declared dependency relationship",
        "Record the repository files each node test run executed (NODE_V8_COVERAGE) with its result, for change impact",
        "With a change set (verify --change), run only the evidence of the claims the change re-marks and reuse the results the last verification recorded fresh (cli/evidence-run.js)",
        "Report for each theorem check the defining file, the Exegra declarations its statement uses with their files, the statement hash with binder names erased, and, for a claim's supersedes theorem, whether it is a kernel-checked implication from the new statement whose conclusion hash is recorded",
        "Extract the static structure of the implementation (tools/extract.js, over the surface of tools/surface.js): per file its digest and its imports, re-exports and dynamic imports (JavaScript), import lines (Lean) and module-level mod and use (Rust), resolved to files, with the extractor identity and version, into specs/<project>/extracted/facts.json; and the observed facts of a recorded session (tools/observe.js). Static extraction establishes static structure only and is never presented as runtime behavioural fidelity"
      ],
      "unknowns": [
        "Only evidence of kind test is executed; measurement, document and review evidence stay author-entered.",
        "The traceability check compares paths only: it does not check that a module implements what its component claims, nor that relationships match imports. Its surface is src/, cli/ and tools/ with the extensions .js, .json, .css and .html, plus index.html and vite.config.js: a .mjs file is outside it (tools/bench-mm1.mjs was unclaimed until this correction), and formal/ and engine/ are outside it too, so an unclaimed Lean or Rust file is not reported.",
        "Browser tests need Chrome and the Vite development server; `verify --skip-browser` skips them and records their evidence as not run, unless its earlier result was recorded on the same tree stamp.",
        "A whole-file evidence reference to a test file with a test that skips itself where a tool is missing (Lean, a native binary) is not a pass in such an environment; the reference passes only where every matched test runs.",
        "The Lean checker does not yet report implemented_by, extern or partial for a definition (tools/lean-theorems.js reports kind, axioms, the kernel check, the constants in the statement and the statement text), so only opaque constants are refused for that reason today."
      ],
      "implementation": {
        "status": "manual",
        "modules": [
          "tools/traceability.js",
          "tools/lean-theorems.js",
          "tools/tree-stamp.js",
          "tools/outcomes-node-reporter.js",
          "tools/outcomes-playwright-reporter.js",
          "tools/run-unit-tests.js",
          "cli/outcomes.js",
          "tools/import-scan.js",
          "cli/evidence-run.js",
          "tools/extract.js",
          "tools/surface.js",
          "tools/observe.js"
        ],
        "notes": "Orchestrated by the verify command in cli/commands.js (claimed by agent-cli).",
        "language": "js",
        "trusts": [
          "trusted-lean-kernel"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "spec-checker",
      "name": "Specification checker",
      "parent": "tooling",
      "category": "infrastructure",
      "runsIn": "node",
      "purpose": "A read-only command that prints a specification file's diagnostics, scenario outcomes and claim results, and optionally a trace.",
      "implementation": {
